     "title": "At the threshold",
     "years": "c. 1300 - 1430",
     "text": "Before the Renaissance had a name, painters began to give figures weight and a place to stand. Giotto's mourners lean in; Masaccio builds a chapel in paint; in Bruges, van Eyck paints a room and everything in it.",
