    },
    {
     "title": "Florence, 1430-1500",
     "years": "The Early Renaissance",
     "text": "Perspective, anatomy and the old myths come back. Botticelli paints goddesses for the Medici; Mantegna foreshortens a dead Christ so sharply that the feet fill the picture. The space opens up.",
